OL,3,GNEWSA'My treatment was a miracle,' says
OL,4,Astroke patient as new 24-hour service
OL,5,Arolled out
OL,6,
OL,7,FWhen Gemma O'Hara woke up in the night
OL,8,Fwith "intense pain" in her neck,
OL,9,Fsickness and vertigo she knew something
OL,10,Fwas "not right".
OL,12,FThe 40-year-old, who had just come back
OL,13,Ffrom holiday, had suffered a brain stem
OL,14,Fstroke.
OL,16,FGemma was able to have a thrombectomy,
OL,17,Fwhich removes blood clots and restores
OL,18,Fblood flow to the brain, a procedure
OL,19,Fshe has said is a "miracle treatment"
OL,20,Fthat has enabled her to recover well.
OL,23,APub: 05-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
